  "title": "Sidereus Nuncius (Galileo, 1610)",
  "summary": "Galileo's Sidereus Nuncius was printed in Venice in 1610, with the imprint of Tommaso Baglioni. It reported his telescope observations of Jupiter's four largest moons, which he named the Medicean stars after the Grand Duke of Tuscany. Linda Hall Library says this showed Earth was not the only centre of motion.",
